  "id": "erp",
  "term": "ERP",
  "definition": "ERP, or event-related potential, is a measure of brain electrical activity recorded from the scalp in response to a specific stimulus or targeted brain event. It is derived by averaging repeated EEG recordings and is used to examine the timing of sensory and cognitive processes, with applications in psychological and clinical assessment.",
